Start the simulation service:
bash start_env.sh configs/environment.json

Start the local model server in a second terminal:
./scripts/serve_qwen_vllm.sh

Start Pi in a third terminal:
./scripts/install_pi.sh   # once
./scripts/run_pi_agent.sh
Pi will read the vending SKILL.md, create an environment with POST /env, and call its actions through the REST API.
While Pi is running, its terminal is the live view. Its full trace is saved as JSONL under:
runs/pi-sessions/
To make a shareable visual trace, use Pi’s /export command before quitting:
/export /workspaces/VendingBenchSimplified/runs/pi-session.html
The existing dashboard command:
./scripts/view_runs.sh